        "Jun Ye"
      ],
      "assessment": {
        "nobel_worthiness": "Optical lattice clocks have produced an extraordinary advance in precision measurement and access to new tests and applications.",
        "attribution": "Katori originated the magic-wavelength lattice-clock concept, and Ye made decisive experimental advances and demonstrations.",
        "maturity": "Independent laboratories have reached remarkable performance and the technique is mature, reproducible, and influential.",
        "uncertainties": [
          "The eventual scientific prize framing may need to distinguish the clock concept from the broader precision-metrology programme."
        ]
      }
    },
