        "Alan H. Guth",
        "Andrei Linde",
        "Viatcheslav Mukhanov"
      ],
      "assessment": {
        "nobel_worthiness": "Inflation and the quantum origin of structure provide a deep and powerful account of the observed Universe.",
        "attribution": "Guth initiated inflation, Linde made essential theoretical developments, and Mukhanov provided decisive treatment of primordial perturbations.",
        "maturity": "Cosmological observations strongly support key consequences, and the framework has shaped modern cosmology for decades.",
        "uncertainties": [
          "No direct primordial gravitational-wave signature has yet singled out an inflationary mechanism.",
          "Theoretical attribution and the relation between broad framework and specific models warrant scrutiny."
        ]
      }
    },
    {
